"text","text":"An Origami → SwiftUI translator: a deterministic parser reads Facebook’s "},{"code":".origami","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"patch graph into a semantic IR, and a codegen writes that IR out as SwiftUI. Swami"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"is also the patch-matched helper library that fills gaps between Origami patches"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and native SwiftUI — one helper per Origami patch, named after the patch, sized by"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Origami’s patch surface. Every pattern that lands is a deliverable, verified against"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Origami’s own render, and shipped as a DocC-embedded example."}],"title":"Swami"},"doc://samatwork.Swami/documentation/Swami/Interaction_DragView/accessibilityRotor(_:textRanges:)-948r9":{"fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"accessibilityRotor","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"L","kind":"genericParameter"},{"text":">(","kind":"text"},{"text":"L","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"textRanges","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": [","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:Sn","text":"Range","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"String","preciseIdentifier":"s:SS"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Index","preciseIdentifier":"s:SS5IndexV"},{"kind":"text","text":">]) -> "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"some"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"View","preciseIdentifier":"s:7SwiftUI4ViewP"}],"kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/swami\/interaction_dragview\/accessibilityrotor(_:textranges:)-948r9","type":"topic","abstract":[],"role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/samatwork.Swami\/documentation\/Swami\/Interaction_DragView\/accessibilityRotor(_:textRanges:)-948r9","title":"accessibilityRotor(_:textRanges:)"},"doc://samatwork.Swami/documentation/Swami/Interaction_DragView":{"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"Interaction_DragView","kind":"identifier"}],"fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Interaction_DragView","kind":"identifier"}],"type":"topic","title":"Interaction_DragView","identifier":"doc:\/\/samatwork.Swami\/documentation\/Swami\/Interaction_DragView","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/swami\/interaction_dragview","abstract":[{"text":"Drags a layer in any direction with momentum and rubber-band bounds. The draggable","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"card responds to touch input via Origami’s ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"origami.Drag"},{"text":" patch, which wires its","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"output ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Position"},{"text":" to the layer’s transform. When released near the center, the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"card snaps back to its resting position.","type":"text"}]}}}